---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Evidence | LoanSlam"
  description="LoanSlam evaluates route safety and response quality through synthetic journeys, trace review, and model comparison."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
      <h1>Quality is measured in conversations, not claims.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The site reflects the project posture: build narrow, test the real turn path, and keep
        failures visible enough to fix.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container evidence-grid">
      <article class="evidence-item" id="journeys">
        <p class="eyebrow">Journey suites</p>
        <h2>Synthetic users push the route map.</h2>
        <p>
          Scenario runs exercise normal questions, account-specific requests, vulnerable-customer
          signals, and excluded topics. Passing means the engine chooses the right envelope, not
          that it recites a fixed sentence.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="evidence-item" id="traces">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trace review</p>
        <h2>Every turn leaves something inspectable.</h2>
        <p>
          The review surface keeps the planner proposal, retrieval context, validator decision, and
          final response together. That makes regressions easier to explain and harder to hide.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="evidence-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">Model comparison</p>
        <h2>Candidate planners compete on behavior.</h2>
        <p>
          Model choice is treated as an empirical question. The useful model is the one that gives
          the validator good proposals across the messy cases, not just the easy demo prompt.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
